ls with removable safeguards are irresponsible, a week after Meta released its own Muse Spark Open.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/bill-gates-is-a-fan-of-metas-ai-agent-muse-says-i-talked-to-alexandr-wang-about-it-congratulated-him-and-even-though-/articleshow/135208987.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/bill-gates-is-a-fan-of-metas-ai-agent-muse-says-i-talked-to-alexandr-wang-about-it-congratulated-him-and-even-though-/articleshow/135208987.cms]]></guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:52:49 +0530</pubDate><dc:creator>TOI TECH DESK</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" length="998403" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135209071,imgsize-998403.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US court says detained migrants have no constitutional right to bond hearings]]></title><description><![CDATA[The US Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit has made a pivotal ruling concerning immigrant detention, involving three men who unlawfully entered the country. The court decided to overturn earlier decisions that allowed them individualized bond hearings while awaiting removal proceedings. This change stirs substantial dialogue on the potential impacts on the constitutional rights of immigrants facing detention without due process.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-us-appeals-court-ruled-10-7-that-immigrants-detained-after-entering-the-country-illegally-are-not-constitutionally-entitled-to-bond-hearings-reversing-a-july-ruling-affecting-texas-louisiana-and-mississippi/articleshow/135206252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-us-appeals-court-ruled-10-7-that-immigrants-detained-after-entering-the-country-illegally-are-not-constitutionally-entitled-to-bond-hearings-reversing-a-july-ruling-affecting-texas-louisiana-and-mississippi/articleshow/135206252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21: